<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 75,332 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 75,332 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 75,332 tonnes of export and import cargo in 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Tuesday, compared to 110,478 tonnes on Monday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Tuesday	  Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			18,773	    9,448</p>
<p>    Import cargo			66,559	  101,030</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, seven ships sailed and seven berthed. In the next 24 hours, six ships were expected to sail and eight were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity		Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		  Berthing</p>
<p>Crude oil		67,603	 Johar		30/10</p>
<p>Jet fuel		 25,000	 Chilham Castle     due</p>
<p>Sugar		     1,400	 Gemstar-1	    due</p>
<p>High speed deisel    52,000	 Al-Maqwa	   31/10</p>
<p>Fertilizer	     31,802	 Cargo Explorer    1/11</p>
<p>Jute			5,419	 Al-Salma	     due</p>
<p>Sulphur		   5,000	 Calimenesti	  due</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
